The toolchain audit (session spec-isa-audit, 2026-10-28), third part:
forms only the vendor assembler emits whose printed form is explicit but
a detail of whose result the toolchain leaves open; each detail is the
choice below, recorded as an open question (HARDWARE-SPEC Q-31 to Q-33):

- `d2 e1` / `d3 e1` (`d2 f1`, `d3 f1` a pair's head): rD = rH_rL >> n
  or >>> n rounded up, to nearest with ties up, to nearest with ties to
  even, or toward zero, then saturated into rD as the plain `de` / `df`
  forms are; n 0 to 63 (`d2`: bits 16-19 and 24-25; `d3`: a register's
  bits 0-5).
- The multiplies with a memory operand (`e0..ee ee`, `60..6e ee`,
  `e0..ee e8`, `6x|ex e9|ec|ed`): rH_rL (=|+=|-=) the first operand,
  a word or (`h[`) a halfword, times a register or a word; the vendor
  assembler counts the first increment in the first operand's size and
  the second's in words, so `h[` is the first operand only. (s) signed,
  (u) unsigned, for the halfword's extension and the product. Both
  addresses are the registers before the instruction; the increments
  follow (the first, then the second), and the pair is written last.
- `60 e8 00 DI` rD = [npc + rI] and `aD ff <imm32>` rD = [npc + #i]:
  npc taken as the next instruction's address. The table took the
  6-byte one for another class that ended the run.
- `70 e0 40 DS` (`70 f0`): rD = rS with its halves swapped, the
  halfword counterpart of `70 e0 00`'s byte reversal.

Decoded before the table, by the vendor decoder table's masks. The crate
tests pair_shifts_with_rounding, memory_multiplies and
npc_loads_and_the_halves_swap, and the harness test
forms_with_an_open_detail (tests/images/isaops.S), fail without it. From
the vendor toolchain (PROVENANCE P-1, P-64) only.

